# A line starting with `@` continues the expression before it as if the lines
# were joined. After a call whose last argument is a lambda, that is the call:
# its closing parenthesis ended the lambda's body, so the mapped Array is
# threaded, not each element.
#= {result: 2, inputs: {xs: [[1, 2, 3], [4]]}}
map(xs, fn x -> x)
@ len()
